well this is such an honor i have to  tell you this is my first face-to-face  interview in like a year and a half so  to do with an icon like yourself just  feels incredibly special how does it  feel for you to be back and celebrating  art at a place like tiff where you have  been many years i've been here many  years but it is also my first live  interview  in 18 months so i'm so grateful to be  here see your shining face and i  couldn't be happier to be here in  toronto for the film festival which i  love and respect and have been here so  many times with  all sort of all my favorite movies  um  and uh i've worked in canada so much  um so to you know to be able to come  here in person and see it in a film in a  theater tonight with actual real human  beings i'm like  heaven it's not happening yeah it is  heaven this film the good house is  incredible your performance in this  blew me away i think this film really  speaks to a lot of people  a lot of people  have people in their lives who struggle  with addiction and mental health and  those types of things when you were  first approached with this what was it  that drew you to this character  well hildy's just great company  you know she's just like a dane  and she's sort of like a good time girl  kind of friend you'd like to go out  you know and have a few drinks with at  the local bar  and what i what you know as a  an actor of my age  to to get a role where  i can  speak directly to the audience and say  you know like  look at the  look at what the state my life is in now  just you know  i thought it was so liberating for me  and also she's so funny and i do love  comedy more than anything  and i had a great cast i had kevin klein  and rob delaney and marina bakaran and i  mean it was just  we had a wonderful  canadian cast canadian crew  you know it was just a heaven job  you and kevin have quite a history  together like what is that relationship  like you've worked together  over the last few decades is it to like  kind of like a brother-sister friendship  at this point now or is it do you bounce  off of each other a lot i would say we  went to buying drama schools so there is  still that  sort of  my training's better than yours kind of  thing so we have that little competitive  spark  but other than that it is very much  um  [Music]  he teases me to death which always makes  me laugh because he's so funny um  but there's great affection there and i  think great trust  and i was thrilled he did this we've  never seen kevin kline like this before  frank the garbage man and so in a way  it's our favorite romance together  because we're actually  you know we  we do care about each other and  we're meant to be together and  it just has its ups and downs you know  but it was great fun great fun to be  there  yeah that chemistry between you two and  this is great uh what i love about the  film is breaking that fourth wall when i  was sitting down and watching it i just  didn't expect it because it's not  something you typically see in a film  and as a actor you're trained like do  not look dead into the camera you know  so for you to wrap your brain around  that what was that like for you was it a  bit of a weird experience to just kind  of look directly down that lens well you  know  it's funny because in in traditional  theater and shakespeare or whatever  you're always talking to the audience  you're always like listen you know the  truth is that it's like this and the  audience is always on your side when you  do those asides  um they're always in that dilemma with  you and so it felt completely natural to  me  who does hildy have to talk to except  her dogs  and a bottle nobody  so for me to be able to look at look  into the camera and go  thank god you're there can you believe  this you know it's just is this too much  can i please have a drink at the end of  the day  you know and i i so rooted for hildy to  have that drink  you know  gosh she supports everyone in her family  and  all this you know she's clawed her way  up to where she is now  and um  he's trying so hard not to drink  you know she just deserves a break at  the end of the day  um so it was great to be able to look at  the camera and just  in her own very  you know  dark funny way just say  are you watching this do you hear what  i'm hearing you know yeah  i love tilde like very flawed of course  but also a heart of gold like she's  really trying to help her children help  everyone around her do you see a bit of  your own self in that character in that  way  i'd love to be more like hildy  sometimes i'm so serious when i try to  help people  but i guess she is too no i guess there  was so much for me to relate to in  in hilde um  i have a lot of my family members are  actual mormons  so  if i go to a wedding there's often  nothing to drink there so i begin to  feel like  there's a drink i just want a glass of  champagne  so um i think i related to that  and just  you know her  the voice of this woman in her 60s who's  still trying to stay on top of things  it's a voice you don't often hear from  in films um  and uh and you just go yeah guildy we  put it out there man  and i just think he root for her and it  as i said it's a voice you don't hear  from much yeah you've had this  incredible career like it's pretty  incredible what you've achieved so far  i'm always curious as an actor i'm sure  you get lots of stuff coming your way  sent to you  what does a role have to have at this  point in your career  to make you be interested in it because  i'm sure you're like nope do a lot of  things at this point well i am fortunate  that i get to read a bunch of things  i think it's either i fall in love or i  don't  and in this case  even though the character of hildy  really  drew me the film always has to be about  something more than just the characters  and this film is  um  it's about sort of  you know this woman's struggle just to  stay on top of things  uh  and um so i i guess i do  but  that being said  that sort of um  thing takes me lots of different  directions i'm about to go to australia  to play a farmer  you know and then after that i'm going  to be playing a um  a sort of grand dom and then after that  i'm going to be playing like a  british  double 07 sort of person so i'm jumping  around a lot and i must say i'm having a  great time i love that there's another  project coming out that is like so dear  to my heart it will be in ghostbusters  afterlife which is crazy to me that you  know 37 years later i know you'll be  back in this character like what does  that feel like for you because i'm  assuming at the time when that those  films were made you didn't know the  legacy that they would have  no of course we didn't think of of that  we just wanted to make a wonderful film  and in those days you didn't really make  sequels  i think that for us it's such a  family  legacy that to work with ivan reitman's  son jason who's done an amazing job and  this sort of came out of his  thinking about ghostbusters and what  would make sense now it's full of heart  it's very funny it's very charming and  it will surprise everybody it's just a  glorious film  i'm super excited to see it anytime i  see those films on television i don't  care how many times i've watched them i  watch it and it's always like a saturday  afternoon or sunday afternoon when  you've done so much in your career i'm  always curious and i love asking people  this like when's the last time you sat  down and watched something of yourself  on tv like has anything been on where  you were like oh and are you able to  watch yourself on screen because a lot  of people can't like me i'm like i don't  want to look at myself yeah  i think i'll find out tonight because  i'll get to watch the good house with  actual real people  in the theater and that will be  wonderful because for the comedy you  really need an audience and as much as  i've appreciated having good  entertainment at home during the last 18  months  it's exciting to be in a theater with  fellow human beings  so i think i'll try to watch tonight  i think i'll enjoy it  but  frankly i don't sit around watching  things i've done  i have some of the movies but i think my  daughter  she had to see alien at someone else's  house  when she was 12 or something like that  and i don't keep them lying around i  thought this will scare her you know so  ghostbusters actually i let her see of  course of course well it has been an  honor to talk to you thank you so much  for joining bt canada i can't wait for  everybody to see the good house because  i think honestly after the last year and  a half that we've had a lot of people  are really gonna connect with this film  and you know what i wish we could grab a  glass of red wine together sometime but  maybe next week maybe next time next  time such a pleasure to talk to you  dallas thank you for having me an honor  thank you so much  you
 

